;; A shelf: books, each with an :id that names it here and in the cache
;; (<id>.pdf), a :title, and the reason it is on the shelf. :file is what
;; the book is called in the owner's library, and is the only line that is
;; about one person's disk: someone else keeps the ids and puts their own
;; file names there, or drops a PDF named <id>.pdf into the cache's pdf/. This one is the workshop's own subjects,
;; read back out of the owner's library: graphs, agents, the cloud it ran
;; on, the telemetry we added, and the language it was all written in.
;; There is no Emacs book in the library. The Lisp one stands in.
